Looking at the skill context, it says:
```csharp
Assert.StartsWith("prefix", actualString);
Assert.EndsWith("suffix", actualString);
Assert.MatchesRegex(@"\d{3}-\d{4}", phoneNumber);
```

These might be available in a newer version of MSTest. Let me check what's available. The error says `Assert` doesn't contain these definitions. These APIs might be in MSTest 3.9+ or 4.x.
I should look into which MSTest versions support these assertion methods.

